{% from '_macros.j2' import section %}
{% set bypass_method = finding.extra.get('method') or finding.extra.get('technique') or 'see evidence' %}
{{ section(idx, finding, severity_label, repro_curl,
    suggested_title="403/401 bypass on " ~ finding.url ~ " via " ~ (bypass_method|string),
    impact=(
"A path that returns 403 / 401 through the normal request flow is reachable via a bypass technique (path-segment "
"trick, header injection, alternative method, or proxy-confusion). The protected content is now accessible without "
"the authentication / authorization the developer expected. Severity depends entirely on **what the protected path "
"actually exposes**: admin panel → critical, debug endpoint → high, internal API → high, static directory listing → "
"medium/low."
),
    validation=(
"1. Confirm the bypass response actually returns the protected content, not just a different error page.\n"
"2. Diff the bypassed response against an authenticated response from a low-privilege user. If they match, the "
"   bypass is real but the content is non-sensitive.\n"
"3. Identify exactly **what data / functionality** the bypassed path exposes. The impact statement in your "
"   submission must be `<specific data> / <specific action> exposed`, not `403 bypassed`.\n"
"4. Test whether the bypass is reproducible from a clean IP (sometimes WAFs whitelist your IP after early probes, "
"   making the bypass an artifact of your testing flow rather than a real issue)."
),
    note=(
"This finding class is downgraded hard when the \"protected\" path doesn't actually contain anything sensitive. "
"Confirm the impact before reporting — \"the path returns content\" is not enough."
)
) }}
